# Every text file is LF in the repo and on checkout. A file saved as CRLF on
# Windows (src/shop.ts in 2859cde) made later merges conflict across the whole
# file, so git normalises them all.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The tests compare these committed fixtures byte for byte with a fresh build
# (test/shop.test.ts), so they stay LF on every checkout: a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise turn them into CRLF and fail that test.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
web/shop/catalog.json text eol=lf
# A recording's manifest hashes steps.json byte for byte (SPEC §7), so a CRLF
# checkout would make every recording refuse to load.
demo/recordings/**/*.json text eol=lf

# Photos and renders are bytes; their hashes are in the receipts.
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
